  "verbalization": "Tranilast, through its indication for Vasomotor Rhinitis and Allergic Rhinitis, appears to be linked to Fluticasone Furoate and Flunisolide, both of which are indicated for Allergic Asthma. This suggests a potential pathway where Tranilast may influence the respiratory system via these corticosteroid agents, possibly by modulating inflammatory responses. The shared indication of Allergic Asthma across multiple paths implies a possible mechanism involving inflammation or immune modulation, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Tranilast could contribute to the pathogenesis of Allergic Asthma through indirect pathways involving corticosteroid use, though further research is needed to confirm this relationship.",
